      "object_marking_refs": [
        "marking-definition--613f2e26-407d-48c7-9eca-b8e91df99dc9"
      ],
      "abstract": "RISK-001 evidence for 127.0.0.1:8787",
      "content": "Observation: The catalog contains tools that read private data (list_customers, get_notes), tools that accept unconstrained external input (fetch_url) and tools that can send data outward (fetch_url, send_email).\nInference: A single injected instruction reaching the ingress tool could move data from the reader to the egress tool. This is a structural risk indicator inferred from tool metadata, not an observed exploit.\nRecommendation: Separate private-data readers from egress tools across servers, require explicit confirmation before outbound actions, and scope credentials per tool rather than per server.\nLimitations: Capability classes are inferred from tool names, descriptions and annotations; they may be wrong. | No tool was invoked, so no data flow was observed. | A trifecta indicator is not a vulnerability and must not be reported as one.\nEvidence: tools/list → capability composition",
      "object_refs": [
        "infrastructure--ee142666-9769-5802-9bd3-3ad14485d499",
        "vulnerability--8774ea0c-a427-5c73-a45e-d92e28cca840"
