      ],
      "abstract": "TOOL-002 evidence for 127.0.0.1:8787",
      "content": "Observation: 1 metadata field matched narrow injection heuristics: tools[get_notes].description (instruction-override, credential-path).\nInference: Text in tool metadata may be intended to steer the model rather than describe the tool. This is a signal, not proof of malice.\nRecommendation: Review the matched fields manually. If the wording is not justified by the tool's function, treat the server as untrusted until the publisher explains it. Prefer servers that pin tool definitions by hash.\nLimitations: Pattern matching cannot distinguish adversarial metadata from unusual but legitimate documentation. | Novel or paraphrased instructions will not be detected. | Absence of a match is not evidence of safety.\nEvidence: tools[get_notes].description",
      "object_refs": [
