        "marking-definition--613f2e26-407d-48c7-9eca-b8e91df99dc9"
      ],
      "abstract": "TOOL-003 evidence for 127.0.0.1:8787",
      "content": "Observation: 3 of 4 tools accept an unconstrained string parameter; 2 use an object schema without additionalProperties: false. High-impact tools affected: send_email.\nInference: Unconstrained input widens the path from model output to a shell, a query, a filesystem path or an outbound request.\nRecommendation: Set additionalProperties: false and constrain every string parameter with enum, pattern, format or maxLength.\nLimitations: Schema strictness is a proxy: a strict schema does not guarantee safe handling downstream.\nEvidence: tools/list → inputSchema",
      "object_refs": [
        "infrastructure--ee142666-9769-5802-9bd3-3ad14485d499",
        "vulnerability--14f21851-7a52-5ff7-84dc-11ee7ef66853"
