    {
      "type": "note",
      "spec_version": "2.1",
      "id": "note--37ea62cd-eaaa-5e6b-92c1-58a0bb2595be",
      "created": "2026-11-22T15:29:59.824Z",
      "modified": "2026-11-22T15:29:59.824Z",
      "created_by_ref": "identity--83905312-a177-53f3-97cf-eefc65221708",
      "object_marking_refs": [
        "marking-definition--613f2e26-407d-48c7-9eca-b8e91df99dc9"
      ],
      "abstract": "TOOL-001 evidence for 127.0.0.1:8787",
      "content": "Observation: Of 4 tools: 0 have no annotations, 4 have no title, 0 have no description.\nInference: Clients cannot warn users about destructive or open-world behaviour, and LLM tool selection relies on descriptions that are missing.\nRecommendation: Annotate every tool with title, readOnlyHint, destructiveHint, idempotentHint and openWorldHint, and write a description that states when the tool should and should not be used.\nLimitations: Annotations are hints, not enforcement; correct annotation does not imply correct behaviour.\nEvidence: tools/list → annotations/title/description",
